      <Docs>
        <summary>
            Arguments passed to to <see cref="P:Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.Operations.ICollectionExpressionOperation.ConstructMethod" />, if present. Arguments are in evaluation order. This can
            be an empty array. Will never be <see langword="default" />.  If the arguments successfully bound, these will all be
            <see cref="T:Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.Operations.IArgumentOperation" />; otherwise, they can be any operation.
            </summary>
        <value>To be added.</value>
        <remarks>
            If the invocation is in its expanded form, then params/ParamArray arguments would be collected into arrays.
            Default values are supplied for optional arguments missing in source. <para />
            If this is a collection builder method, this will include all arguments to the method,
            except for the final <c>ReadOnlySpan</c> argument that receives the collection elements.
            That final argument will be represented by an <see cref="T:Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.Operations.IArgumentOperation" /> whose 'Value' is an
            <see cref="T:Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.Operations.ICollectionExpressionElementsPlaceholderOperation" />. The actual elements passed
            to the creation method are contained in <see cref="P:Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.Operations.ICollectionExpressionOperation.Elements" />.
            </remarks>
      </Docs>
